        <h1 style="text-align: center;">Hardware Implementation</h1>


        <h2 class="subhead" id="algorithim">Constraints</h1>
        <p>
            This module will take the 1280x720p 60fps video as a input using the the Xilinx RGB video format, then will crop the image to the desired size, 
            then will re-size this sub-image to a 28x28 video stream
            <br> <br>

            Input signals:
            <table>
                <!--<caption>Resizing IP input signals</caption>-->
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th>Interface</th>
                    <th>Signals</th>
                    <th>Description</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <!-- Video input -->
                  <tr>
                    <td>RGB video I/P</td>
                    <td>
                      rgb_i_data[23:0] // R, G, B pixel values - each 1 byte <br>
                      rgb_i_valid // above signal has a valid pixel <br>
                      rgb_i_hsync // pulsed at the end of each horrizontal pixel row (1280) <br>
                      rgb_i_vsync // pulsed at the end of all the horrizontal rows (720) <br>
                    </td>
                    <td> Input vide stream passed from the vivado HDMI IP.</td>
                  </tr>

                  <!-- Video output  -->
                  <tr>
                    <td>RGB video O/P</td>
                    <td>
                      data_o[7:0] // Luminance value <br>
                      valid_o // above signal has a valid pixel <br>
                      vsync_gen_o // pulsed at the end of the frame - no hsync used <br>
                    </td>
                    <td> Output video stream passed to K-Means logic and to DMA </td>
                  </tr>

                  <!-- Control signals  -->
                  <tr>
                    <td>Contol signals</td>
                    <td>
                        clk // Pixel clock <br>
                        resetn // Pixel reset <br>
                        resetn_sub_image_filter // Synchronous reset - for debugging  <br>
                        enable_sub_image_filter // Enable Resizing / video output <br>
                    </td>
                    <td> clock, reset and enable signals</td>
                  </tr>

                  <!-- Sub-region control  -->
                  <tr>
                    <td>Sub-region control / Crop box</td>
                    <td>
                      top_left_x_0[15:0] //  <br>
                      top_left_y_0[15:0] //  <br>
                      bot_right_x_0[15:0] // unsigned int value, between 0-1279  <br>
                      bot_right_y_0[15:0] // unsigned int value, between 0-719 <br>
                      update_0 // To indicate a new sub-box is desired.<br>
                    </td>
                    <td> Sub-region control </td>
                  </tr>

                </tbody>
              </table>

        </p>



